{# Modern <source> of a <picture> over an ingested blob.

   MinIO stores images content-addressed with a sibling WebP next to the PNG, so
   the modern candidate is DERIVED from the original path, never carried in the
   payload — by the one owner of that rule, App\Service\Storage\WebpSibling
   (shared with the in-page image refresh endpoint), which answers null for
   anything but a .png so the browser is never pointed at a file that was never
   written (silent 404 inside the <picture>).

   Params: src — browser-ready URL of the original, leading slash included;
           webp — optional explicit candidate (the pending-image template's
           placeholder), bypassing the derivation. #}
{%- set candidate = webp is defined and webp ? webp : webp_sibling(src) -%}
{%- if candidate -%}
    <source srcset="{{ candidate }}" type="image/webp">
{%- endif -%}
